--TEST--
the hover on a restricted method says where it is allowed, the entry's note, and the file and line of the entry, above the method's `///` text, `rule:packaging/a-restriction-limits-where-a-declaration-is-used`
--FILE--
<?nvs
autoload 'App' from './app';

echo App\Secret\Vault::op<|>en(), "\n";
--FILE app/Secret/Vault.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace App\Secret;

final class Vault
{
    /// Opens the vault.
    public static function open(): string
    {
        return "open";
    }
}
--FILE package.toml--
[[restrict]]
use = 'App\Secret\Vault::open'
allow = ['App\Allowed']
note = 'Use `App\Allowed\Door::open`.'
--REQUEST--
hover
--EXPECT--
**Restricted.** It is allowed only in `App\Allowed`. Use `App\Allowed\Door::open`.

This rule is in `package.toml`, line 2.

Opens the vault.
